Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:16:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/23] VideoEncoder: classify the low-latency rtvc session
 honestly, convert only what needs it

With EnableLowLatencyRateControl VideoToolbox serves the session from the rtvc hardware encoder, whose session answers UsingHardwareAcceleratedVideoEncoder with kVTPropertyNotSupportedErr (-12900). The runtime read that as software, warned about it, and - correctly, it turns out - fed it the video-range 4:2:0 conversion: the rtvc encoder, like the software ones, writes a full-range stream for a BGRA source (the encoder test VUI check fails without the conversion). So: session kind from the property when it answers and from the encoder id otherwise (EncoderSessionKind.h, unit-tested), the conversion decided by whether the session keeps video range from BGRA (only the classic ave encoder does), and the init log names the encoder id and says why a hardware session is converted (about 1 ms of submit per frame at 2272x1264).

